### Muonic X-rays from a mu- beam in a 1 cm steel plate lying on the LYSO panel, one job (2026-11-09, the beam study of
### stainless steel: can the panel tell the Fe, Cr and Ni peaks apart; scripts/beam_steel_local.sh writes and runs the
### jobs). The setup of macro/beam_xray_lyso.mac, the 126.88 x 126.88 x 3.18 mm LYSO panel of 20 x 20 pixels with its Al
### top face at 32.5 cm, but with a 20 x 20 x 1 cm plate on the panel (32.5-33.5 cm) in place of the 4 cm target.
### Another panel: bmPanel (macro/panel_<bmPanel>.mac) with its centre at bmPanelZ (cm): lyso 32.332, or czt 32.0 (the
### CZT plane of 4 x 4 pixels of 25 x 25 x 10 mm, its top against the plate; the same study for the CZT, 2026-11-09).
### The mu- beam comes straight down (-z) onto the plate's top face, starting at bmZ (cm), with a Gaussian spot of
### sigma bmSigX x bmSigY (cm; PSI muE1: 39 x 25 mm FWHM = 1.656 x 1.062 cm) and kinetic energy bmEkin (MeV): 29.95 MeV
### (85 MeV/c) stops about 0.8 cm deep in steel, ~2 mm above the panel.
### The muonic X-rays get the measured energies of Cr, Fe and Ni (/tof/physics/muonXrayEnergies measured): the default
### point-nucleus levels put their K lines 11-16% too high.
### As in the Si study, every radioactive decay of the nuclei that the captures leave behind is simulated at its own time;
### analysis/beam_steel_spectrum.C weights such hits by their chance of falling inside the measuring time, and adds the
### panel's own Lu-176 from a decay-only run.
### The job macro sets the target material (/tof/target/material) and the aliases bmSeed, bmEvents, bmDir, bmFile,
### bmEkin, bmSigX, bmSigY, bmZ, bmPanel, bmPanelZ and bmFilter (/EventFilter: 0 writes every event, so that the analysis counts the muons
### each element caught; 8 only the events with energy in the panel and a muon stopped in the target), then executes
### this. Needs TOFmeter --preinit macro/preinit_lyso.mac (radioactive decay and fluorescence).
/tof/det/worldSize 420 420 300 cm
/tof/det/stack false
/tof/target/size 20 20 1 cm
/tof/target/position 0 0 33.0 cm
/control/execute macro/panel_{bmPanel}.mac
/tof/czt/position 0 0 {bmPanelZ} cm
/update
/tof/physics/muonXrayEnergies measured
/OutputFormat 1
/EventFilter {bmFilter}
/OutputDirectory {bmDir}
/OutputFile {bmFile}
/gun/seed {bmSeed}
/GeneralParticleSource 1
/gps/particle mu-
/gps/pos/type Beam
/gps/pos/centre 0 0 {bmZ} cm
/gps/pos/sigma_x {bmSigX} cm
/gps/pos/sigma_y {bmSigY} cm
/gps/direction 0 0 -1
/gps/ene/type Mono
/gps/ene/mono {bmEkin} MeV
# Auger electrons off (the radioactive decay turned them on), as in the Si study: their few keV stay in the pixel
# anyway, and they make the run 1.5 times slower. Fluorescence (K X-rays that can leave a pixel) stays on.
/process/em/auger false
/process/em/augerCascade false
# verbose 1: the log ends with "Number of events processed : <bmEvents>", which scripts/beam_steel_local.sh looks for
/run/verbose 1
/run/printProgress 100000
/run/beamOn {bmEvents}
